  "headline": "On the UNREPAIRED arm the predeclared blindness signature is ABSENT: gates 17.4, 17.6 and 17.8 fail because the diagnostics are not flat. They move, and they move the wrong way. Decision loss rises 4x (0.3328 -> 1.3354) while mean NEES FALLS 20% (1.7246 -> 1.3768, slope -0.2961, three times its margin) and coverage IMPROVES (0.9678 -> 0.9784). An operator watching self-consistency would see calibration improving exactly as decisions became catastrophically wrong. That is not blindness; it is anti-correlation, which is worse.",
